23
00:01:37,700 --> 00:01:42,200
这是因为智能体已经被部署在医疗 金融 甚至
This is because agents are being deployed in healthcare and finance and even in the

24
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:45,880
军事等领域 在这些场景中一旦出错后果会非常灾难性
military, where it's catastrophic if things go wrong.

25
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:50,700
传统上我们谈论的范式是评估（eval）
The traditional paradigm we've been talking about is evals,

26
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:55,680
也就是你有一组测试输入 想看看智能体会给出什么样的输出
where you have this sort of test input and you want to see what is the output that comes

27
00:01:55,680 --> 00:01:56,980
看看智能体会产出什么结果
out from the agent.

28
00:01:57,080 --> 00:01:58,080
你会有这样一整套数据
You have a set of these,

29
00:01:58,220 --> 00:01:59,860
你可能会称之为黄金数据集
maybe you call it a golden dataset.

30
00:02:00,660 --> 00:02:04,300
但在这个新的范式下 仅靠评估（eval）已经远远不够
But evals, they just aren't enough with this new paradigm.

31
00:02:05,180 --> 00:02:07,700
随着智能体能力越来越强
As agents become more and more capable,

32
00:02:08,180 --> 00:02:12,260
会出现越来越多有趣但未定义的行为
there's more and more interesting undefined behavior that can happen.

33
00:02:12,260 --> 00:02:16,660
比如 智能体可以从一组不同的工具中进行调用
For example, agents can call from a set of different tools.

34
00:02:17,260 --> 00:02:19,460
有时候工具的数量还在指数级增长
Sometimes the number of tools is growing exponentially.

35
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:22,500
它们可以调用不同的记忆源
They can call from different memory sources.

36
00:02:23,140 --> 00:02:24,960
它们可以调用自己的子智能体
They can call their own sub-agents,

37
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:28,660
而这些子智能体又有自己的工具和记忆源
which those sub-agents have their own tools and memory sources,

38
00:02:29,260 --> 00:02:31,120
并且还能递归地再拥有自己的子智能体
and recursively can have their own sub-agents.

39
00:02:31,820 --> 00:02:34,320
随着时间推移 这一切只会变得更加复杂
This is just becoming more complicated with time,

40
00:02:34,380 --> 00:02:37,340
在这种组合爆炸式的输入空间下
and with this combinatorial sort of input space,

41
00:02:37,340 --> 00:02:42,400
仅仅准备一套输入输出测试已经完全不够用了
just having a set of tests for input and output doesn't cut it anymore.

42
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:48,940
你根本不可能覆盖到你想要的所有边界情况
There's no way you can hit all of the edge cases that you would want to here.

43
00:02:50,140 --> 00:02:55,060
因此我们需要从测试和评估（eval）范式转向监控范式
And so we go from a testing and evals paradigm to a monitoring paradigm.

44
00:02:55,580 --> 00:02:59,560
回想在有智能体之前构建产品时
And if you think of building products before agents,

45
00:03:00,380 --> 00:03:02,140
测试一直都非常重要
testing was always very important.

46
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:03,700
拥有单元测试等是很重要的
It's important to have your unit tests,

47
00:03:03,820 --> 00:03:07,800
但监控线上生产环境要重要得多
etc., but monitoring production is just infinitely more important,

48
00:03:08,040 --> 00:03:11,500
它能让你迭代更快 并且更好地捕捉长尾问题
and it allows you to move faster and be better at catching the long tail.

49
00:03:12,640 --> 00:03:15,960
我们认为在某种程度上这可能有点争议
And we think in some ways this is kind of controversial,

50
00:03:16,360 --> 00:03:18,860
